hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5357","“Whoever drinks wine and gets drunk, his prayer will not be accepted for forty days, and if he dies he will enter Hell, but if he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. If he drinks wine again and gets drunk, his prayer will not be accepted for forty days, and if he dies he will enter Hell, but if he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. If he drinks wine again and gets drunk, his prayer will not be accepted for forty days, and if he dies he will enter Hell, but if he repents Allah will accept his repentance. But if he does it again, then Allah will most certainly make him drink of the mire of the puss or sweat on the Day of Resurrection.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is the mire of the pus or sweat? He said: “The drippings of the people of Hell.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3377)"
"5358","narrates: Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) delivered a sermon to us on the pulpit of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), praising and glorifying Allah Almighty, then stated: When the command regarding the prohibition of alcohol was revealed, it was being made from five things: grapes, dates, honey, wheat, and barley. As for khamr, it is called for everything that covers the intellect."
"5359","I heard 'Umar b. Khattab delivering sermon on the pulpit ol Messenger of Allah ﷺ and saying': Now, coming to the point, O people, there was revealed (the command pertaining to the prohibition of wine) and it was prepared (at that time) out of five things: grape, date, honey, wheat, barley, and wine is that which clouds the intellect, and, O people, I wish Messenger of Allah ﷺ had explained to us in greater detail three things: the inheritance of the grandfather, of one who dies without leaving any issue, and some of the problems of interest. (Using translation from Muslim 3032b)"
"5360","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every intoxicating substance is forbidden, and it is incumbent upon Allah that whoever drinks an intoxicating substance, Allah will make him drink 'Tibyat al-Khabal' on the Day of Resurrection."
"5361","Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah bin Jarrah (may Allah be pleased with him), Sayyiduna Suhail bin Baida (may Allah be pleased with him), and Sayyiduna Ub"
"5362","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I was serving Fadheekh (a type of wine) to my uncles because I was the youngest among them in age. During this, a person came and said: Wine has been declared unlawful. So they said: O Anas! Throw it away. So I threw it away. The narrator named Sulaiman says: I inquired, what was that wine made from? Sayyiduna Anas replied: From dried and fresh dates. The narrator states: Abu Bakr bin Anas narrated that at that time, wine was made from th"
"5363","I was serving nabidh made from dried and fresh dates to Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him), Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah (may Allah be pleased with him), Sayyiduna Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him), and Sayyiduna Suhail bin Bayda (may Allah be pleased with him). During this, a caller announced: ""Beware! Alcohol has been declared unlawful."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: By Allah, they did not wait to verify whether this news was true or false. They said, ""O Anas! Pour it out,"" so I poured it out. By Allah, after that, these people never turned to alcohol again until their deaths. In those days, alcohol was made from dried and fresh dates."
"5364","I was serving drink to Abu 'Ubaida b. jarrah, Abu Talha and Ubayy b. Ka'b prepared from unripe dates and fresh dates when a visitor came and he said: Verily liquor has been prohibited. Thereupon, Abu Talha said: Anas, stand up and break this pitcher. I stool up and (took hold) of a pointed stone and struck the pitcher with its lower part until it broke into pieces. (Using translation from Muslim 1980g)"
"5365","The first to ask about this were the delegation of the tribe of Abdul Qais, who asked the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Do not drink from dabba’, muzaffat, and hantam (named vessels), and do not drink from a pitcher; rather, drink from water skins. The people said: What if the drink (nabidh) in the water skin becomes strong? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If the drink in the water skin becomes strong, then add water to it. They said: What if it still remains strong? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then pour it out. Then he said: Indeed, Allah the Exalted has made it unlawful for me. (The narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) Allah the Exalted has made wine, gambling, and kubah unlawful, and every intoxicating thing is also unlawful. Sufyan, the narrator, says: I asked Ali bin Badhimah: What is meant by kubah? He said: The drum."
"5366","Every intoxicant is Khamr and every intoxicant is forbidden. He who drinks wine in this world and dies while he is addicted to it, not having repented, will not be given a drink in the Hereafter. (Using translation from Muslim 2003a)"
"5367","narrates: Some people from Yemen came to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). The Prophet (peace be upon him) taught them about the Sunnah and obligatory prayers. Those people said: O Messenger of Allah, there is a drink among us which we make from wheat and barley. The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked, ""Are you asking about Ghubeera?"" They replied, ""Yes."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Do not consume it."" After two days, they again mentioned this matter before the Prophet (peace be upon him), so the Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Are you asking about Ghubeera?"" They replied, ""Yes."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Do not consume it."" When those people intended to depart, they again inquired about this from the Prophet (peace be upon him), so the Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Are you asking about Ghubeera?"" They replied, ""Yes."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Do not consume it."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Umar bin Hakam is Umar bin Hakam bin Thawban, who is an ally of the Aws tribe and is among the distinguished individuals of the people of Madinah. He has heard hadith from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), and Sayyidah Umm Habibah (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"5368","""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Every intoxicant is Khamr and every intoxicant is unlawful.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5585)"
"5369","""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Every intoxicant is Khamr and every intoxicant is unlawful.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5585)"
"5370","The Prophet [SAW] forbade a small amount of whatever intoxicates in large amounts. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5609)"
"5371","Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about Bit'i, whereupon he said: Every drink that causes intoxication is forbidden. (Using translation from Muslim 2001a)"
"5372","Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about Bit'i, whereupon he said: Every drink that causes intoxication is forbidden. (Using translation from Muslim 2001a)"
"5373","Give good tidings to the (people). and make things easy (for them), teach (them), and do not repel (them) ; and I think he also said: Cooperate cheerfully with each other. When he (the Holy Prophet) turned his back, Abu Musa returned to him and said: Messenger of Allah, they (the people of Yemen) have a drink which is (made) from honey and which is prepared by cooking it until it coagulates, and Mizr is prepared from barley, whereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Every intoxicant that detains you from prayer is forbidden. (Using translation from Muslim 1733f)"
"5374","“I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Every intoxicant is unlawful for every believer.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3389)"
"5375","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Every intoxicant is unlawful.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3387)"
"5377","""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] sent me to Yemen and I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, there are drinks there which they call Al-Bit' (mead) and Al-Mizr (beer).' He said: 'What is mead (and beer)?' I said: 'A drink made from honey, and beer is made from barley.' He said: 'Every intoxicant is unlawful.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5604)"
"5378","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade making nabidh by mixing dates and raisins together."
"5379","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade mixing of raisins and dried dates: and unripe dates and fresh dates. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3703)"
"5380","Anas b. Malik is reported to have said that Messenger of Allah ﷺ had forbidden to mixture fresh dates and unripe dates and then drinking (the wine prepared out of it), and that was their common intoxicant when liquor was prohibited. (Using translation from Muslim 1981)"
"5381","‘Do not make Nabidh with dried dates and unripe dates together, make Nabidh with each of them on its own.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3396)"
"5382","The Prophet ﷺ said: If a large amount of anything causes intoxication, a small amount of it is prohibited. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3681)"
"5383","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Every intoxicant is forbidden; if a faraq of anything causes intoxication, a handful of it is forbidden. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3687)"
"5384","The people said: It refers to a specific type of jug. Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: Does that drink intoxicate? The people said: If drunk in excess, it intoxicates. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said: Every intoxicating thing is unlawful. Then those people asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) about Nabidh. He said: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was on a journey. When he returned, some of his companions had prepared Nabidh in Naqir, Hantam, and Duba’ (i.e., specific types of vessels). By the order of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), it was poured out. By the order of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), raisins and water were put in a waterskin (to prepare Nabidh). Nabidh was prepared for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) at night, and the next morning he drank it. Then the next night came, then the evening of the following day came. When evening came, he drank it and also gave it to others to drink. When the morning of the next day came, he poured it out."
"5385","Dates were steeped for the Apostel of Allah ﷺ in skin which was tied up at the top and had a mouth. What was steeped in the morning he would drink in the evening and what was steeped in the evening he would drink in the morning. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3711)"
"5386","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was on a journey. When he returned, some of his companions prepared Nabidh in specific types of vessels called Hantam, Naqir, and Duba. By the order of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), it was poured out. Then, by the order of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), raisins and water were put in a waterskin, and Nabidh was prepared for the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) at night. The next morning, he drank it. After that, the next night came. Then the next day came, until when its evening came, he drank it and gave it to the people to drink as well. On the following day, by your order, that Nabidh was poured out in the morning."
"5387","Dates were steeped for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a skin, but when they could not find a skin, they were steeped for him in a small stone vessel. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3702)"
"5388","""I heard 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, delivering a Khutbah on the Minbar of Al-Madinah and he said: 'O people, on the day that the prohibition of Khamr was revealed, it was made from five things: From grapes, dates, honey, wheat and barley. Khamr is that which overcomes the mind.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5578)"
"5389","I met Faleeh. I asked him about this hadith, and he narrated it to me in the same way as Ismail had narrated it. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Ismail is Ismail bin Ayash. We have mentioned him in our book only in this place so that inference may be drawn from it; otherwise, in this narration, our reliance is on the narrator Mansur bin Abu Muzahim, because he heard this hadith from both Faleeh and Ismail. And we have explained the reason for declaring Ismail unreliable in the book al-Majruheen."
"5390","I asked permission to seek forgiveness for my mother, but I was not granted permission, so tears flowed from my eyes due to mercy for her. Because of her being in Hell, I forbade you from three things. I had forbidden you from visiting graves; now you may visit them, for visiting graves increases goodness. I had forbidden you from keeping sacrificial meat for more than three days; now keep it as long as you wish. I had forbidden you from drinking in certain types of vessels; now drink in whatever vessel you wish, but do not drink anything intoxicating."
"5391","I prohibited you from visiting the graves, but (now) you may visit them, and I prohibited you (from eating) the flesh of sacrific- ed animals beyond three days, but now keep it as long as you like. I prohibited you from the use of Nabidh except (that preoared) in dry waterskins. Now drink (Nabidh prepared in any utensil), but do not drink when it becomes intoxicant. (Using translation from Muslim 1977a)"
"5392","Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the drinking place and asked for water. Al-Abbas said, ""O Fadl! Go to your mother and bring water from her for Messenger of Allah ﷺ ."" Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Give me water to drink."" Al-Abbas said, ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! The people put their hands in it."" Messenger of Allah ﷺ again said, 'Give me water to drink. So, he drank from that water and then went to the Zamzam (well) and there the people were offering water to the others and working at it (drawing water from the well). The Prophet ﷺ then said to them, ""Carry on! You are doing a good deed."" Then he said, ""Were I not afraid that other people would compete with you (in drawing water from Zamzam), I would certainly take the rope and put it over this (i.e. his shoulder) (to draw water)."" On saying that the Prophet ﷺ pointed to his shoulder. (Using translation from Bukhārī 1635)"
"5393","That the Prophet ﷺ was asked about Bit' so he said: ""All drinks that intoxicate are unlawful."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1863)"
"5394","I served drink to Messenger of Allah ﷺ in this cup of mine: honey, Nabidh, water and milk. (Using translation from Muslim 2008)"
"5395","The wife of Sayyiduna Abu Usaid (may Allah be pleased with her), Sayyidah Umm Usaid (may Allah be pleased with her), served the food to the people. She had soaked some dates in a stone vessel from the night before. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished eating, that lady brought the drink and especially served it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5396","narrates: Nabidh used to be prepared for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in a stone bowl. He would drink it on the first day, the second day, and until midday on the third day (after that, he would discard it because it would begin to ferment)."
"5397","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""All drinks that produce intoxication are Haram (forbidden to drink). (Using translation from Bukhārī 242)"
"5398","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Wine is made from grape-syrup, raisins, dried dates, wheat, barley, millet, and I forbid you from every intoxicant. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3677)"
"5399","""The Messenger of Allah forbade (eating) animals that had been taken as targets, the milk of Al-Jallalah (animals that eat dung), and drinking directly from water skins."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4448)"
"5400","Ibn Buraidah narrates from his father that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""I had forbidden you from visiting graves. Now you may visit them. I had forbidden you from keeping the meat of sacrifice for more than three days; now keep it as long as you find appropriate. And I had permitted you to drink nabidh only in water skins; now drink (nabidh) in any vessel you wish, but do not drink anything intoxicating."
"5401","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the delegation of the tribe of ‘Abd al-Qays from drinking nabidh (fermented dri"
"5402","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade preparing nabidh in a green jug."
"5403","The narrator says: Then I went to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) and I informed him that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) was asked about the nabidh of a pitcher, and he replied: This is something which Allah and His Messenger have declared haram. So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said: He has spoken the truth. I asked: What is meant by a pitcher? He replied: Anything that is made from clay."
"5404","""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade earthenware jars, Ad-Dubba' (gourds), Al-Muzaffat containers."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5635)"
"5405","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the delegation of the tribe of Abdul Qais: I forbid you from Naqit, Mughīr Hanṭam, Diyā’, and a specific type of water skin. Drink from your water skins and keep their mouths closed."
"5406","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) forbade wearing silk, (wearing) a gold ring, and drinking from Hantham. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah h"
"5407","narrator states:) As for Dubba’, we used to break grapevines and put them in a vessel called Dubba’, then bury it until it would die. As for Hantam, it is a jar in which we used to bring wine from Syria. As for Naqir, the people of Madinah used to take the root of a date-palm, hollow it out, put fresh and dry dates in it, and bury it in the ground until it would die. As for Muzaffat, it refers to a vessel that is coated with pitch."
"5408","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade making Nabidh in Naqir, Muzaffat, Dubba’, and Hantamah. And he said: ‘Every intoxicant is unlawful.”* (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3401)"
"5409","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of knowledge from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \""I had forbidden you from (drinking) nabidh in specific vessels. Beware, vessels do not make anything unlawful, and every intoxicating thing is unlawful.\"""""
"5410","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade (the use of) dubba’ and naqir."
"5411","""I heard 'Abdul-'Aziz - that is, bin Asid At-Tahi from Al-Basrah - say: 'Ibn Az-Zubair was asked about soaking (fruits) in earthenware jars and he said: ""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade us from that."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5618)"
"5412","narrates: When nothing was available to prepare nabidh for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nabidh would be prepared for him in a stone bowl."
"5413","narrates: Nabidh used to be prepared for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in a waterskin; when a waterskin was not available, it was prepared in a stone bowl."
"5414","The goat of Sayyidah Sawdah (may Allah be pleased with her) died. We tanned its skin and used to prepare nabidh in it until that waterskin became old."
"5415","I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden to an eater except it be carrion or flowing blood.” (Then the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said) There is no harm; tan its skin and benefit from it. Sayyidah Sawdah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: So we sent it and its skin was tanned, then we made a water bag from it until it developed a hole."
"5416","The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: Do you have wealth? I replied: Yes. The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: What kind of wealth? I replied: Allah Almighty has granted me all kinds of wealth—camels, slaves, and goats. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: When Allah Almighty has granted you wealth, its sign should be visible on you. The narrator states: I asked: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! What is your opinion about a person with whom I stay as a guest, but he does not honor me nor show hospitality, and then, at another time, he stays with me as a guest—should I repay his behavior? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: No, rather you should show him hospitality. Abu Ahwas ‘Awf bin Malik bin Nadlah’s father was a companion."
"5417","The Prophet (peace be upon him) observed him in the form of a villager with disheveled, dusty hair and asked: Do you have wealth? He replied: Allah Almighty has granted me every kind of wealth. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: When Allah Almighty bestows a blessing upon a servant, He likes that the blessing be visible on that servant."
"5418","I said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Please come to the shade."" The narrator says: The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) dismounted (from his ride). Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I got up and went to my provision bag. I searched in it and found a cucumber. I broke it and then presented it to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) asked, ""Where did you get this from?"" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! We brought it with us from Madinah Munawwarah."" Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We had a companion to whom we would prepare provisions, and he would take our riding animals to graze. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I prepared his provisions, then he loaded them on his back and set off. He had two sheets on his body which had become old. The narrator says: The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) looked at him and asked, ""Does he have no other clothes besides these two sheets?"" Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! He has two more garments in the provisions which I gave him to wear."" The narrator says: The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said, ""Call him and instruct him to wear those clothes."" Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I called him, he wore those two garments, then he was about to leave when the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""What is wrong with him? May Allah strike his neck—is this not better?"" That person heard this and said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), in the way of Allah?"" The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said, ""In the way of Allah."" Then that person was martyred in the way of Allah. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This was the initial intention of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). Zaid bin Aslam heard hadith from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) because Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) passed away in 79 AH, and Aslam passed away around 50 AH during the rule of Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him). Marwan bin Hakam performed his funeral prayer, who was then the governor of Madinah Munawwarah, so this will guide you to this matter. He heard hadith from Sayyiduna Jabir; he was an elderly man, while Zaid bin Aslam passed away in 136 AH. He was of quite advanced age."
"5419","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever has extra luggage should give it to the one who has none, and whoever has extra provisions should give them to the one who has none. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned various types of wealth until we began to feel as if none of us had any right to keep anything extra."
"5420","""When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, would wear a new garment he would mention what it was, whether an 'Imamah, a Qamis, or a Rida', then he would say: Allahumma lakal-hamdu, Anta kasawtanihi, as'aluka khairuhu wa khaira ma suni'a lahu, wa a'udhu bika min sharrihi wa sharri ma suni'a lahu'"" ('O Allah! For You is the praise, You have clothed me, I ask You for its good and the god for which it was made, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil for which it was made.) (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1767)"
"5421","I ask You for its goodness and the goodness for which it was made, and I seek refuge with You from its evil and the evil for which it was made."
"5422","narrates: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) wore a shirt, he would begin from the right side."
"5423","The Prophet ﷺ said: Wear your white garments, for they are among your best garments, and shroud your dead in them. Among the best types of collyrium you use is antimony (ithmid): it clears the vision and makes the hair sprout. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3878)"
"5424","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) permitted marking (i.e., a strip of silk on a garment) as wide as two fingers."
"5425","The Prophet ﷺ entered Mecca in the year of the Conquest while he had a black turben over him. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4076)"
"5426","""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade Ishtimal As-Samma' and wrapping oneself in a single garment (that did not cover the private parts)."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5342)"
"5427","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing two types of clothing. As for “ishtimal as-samma’,” it means: a person wraps a garment around himself in such a way that both its ends are on his shoulders and his side is exposed. The second is: a person wraps a garment around himself in the manner of “ihtiba’” in such a way that no part of the garment covers his private parts."
"5428","Messenger of Allah. why is it that you put it of immediately. whereupon he said: Gabriel forbade me from it (i. e. wearing of Ods garment), and 'Umar came to him weeping and said: Messenger of Allah you disapproved a thing but you gave it to me. What about me, then? Thereupon be (the Holy Prophet) Wd: I did not give it to you to wear it, but I gave you that you might sell it; and so he (Hadrat Umar) sold it for two thousand dirhams. (Using translation from Muslim 2070)"
"5429","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said regarding silk: ""Whoever wears it in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter."
"5430","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave license to 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf and al-Zubair b. al-'Awwam to wear silk shirts during a journey because of an itch which they had. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4056)"
"5431","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave license to 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf and al-Zubair b. al-'Awwam to wear silk shirts during a journey because of an itch which they had. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4056)"
"5432","Anas b. Malik reported that 'Abd al-Rahman b. Auf and Zu'bair. b. 'Awwam complained to Messenger of Allah ﷺ about lice; he granted them concession to wear shirts of silk. (Using translation from Muslim 2076e)"
"5433","The Prophet (peace be upon him) wore it and then performed prayer in i"
"5434","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) took silk and placed it in his right hand, and took gold and placed it in his left hand"
"5435","I heard ʿUmar saying, ""The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Whoever wears silk in this world, shall not wear it in the Hereafter."" This hadith is also narrated through 'Umar ibn al-Khattab. (Using translation from Bukhārī 5834)"
"5440","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade wearing Qassi and Mu'asfar (types of clothes), wearing a gold ring, and recitin"
"5441","'Umar addressed us at a place known as Jabiya (Syria) and he said: Allah's Apostle ﷺ forbade us the wearing of silk but to the extent of two or three fingers or four fingers. (Using translation from Muslim 2069i)"
"5442","I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) hold Sayyiduna Sufyan bin Abu Suhail (may Allah be pleased with him) by his side and say: “O Sufyan! Do not let your lower garment hang (below the ankles), for Allah Almighty will not look with mercy at those who let (their garments) hang below the ankles.”"
"5443","He who trailed his garment out of pride, Allah would not look toward him on the Day of Resurrection. (Using translation from Muslim 2085e)"
"5444","The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."" Abu Bakr said: ""O Messenger of Allah, one side of my Izar slips unless I pay attention to it."" The Prophet [SAW]: ""You are not one of those who do that out of pride."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5335)"
"5445","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held my shin from the middle and said: This is the place for the lower garment; if you"
"5446","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him). I asked: Have you heard the Prophet Muh"
"5447","“I said to Abu Sa’eed: ‘Did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning the lower wrap?’ He said: ‘Yes. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘The lower wrap of the believer should come to mid-calf, but there is no sin on him if it comes between that point and the ankle. But whatever is lower than the ankle is in the Fire.’ And he said three times: ‘Allah will not look at the one who lets his lower wrap drag out of vanity.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3573)"
"5448","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of the calf of my shin - or his shin - and he said: ""This is the place of the Izar, if you must lower it, then the Izar has no right to be on the ankles."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1783)"
"5449","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held my shin from the middle and said: This is the place for the lower garment; if you"
"5450","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be"
"5451","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned lower garment, Umm Salamah, wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, asked him: And a woman, Messenger of Allah? He replied: She may hang down a span. Umm Salamah said: Still it (foot) will be uncovered. He said: Then a forearm's length, nor exceeding it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4117)"
"5452","I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a company of Muzainah and we swore allegiance to him. The buttons of his shirt were open. I swore allegiance to him and I put my hand inside the collar of his shirt and felt the seal. 'Urwah said: I always saw Mu'awiyah and his son opening their buttons of the collar during winter and summer. They never closed their buttons. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4082)"
"5453","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) performing prayer with his button open. I asked him about this, and he rep"
"5454","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reached us while we were in Azerbaijan with Utbah bin Farqad. (It was written in"
"5455","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: When one of you puts on sandals, he should put on his right one first, and when he takes them off, he should take off the left one first ; so that the right one should be the first to be put on and the last to be taken off. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4139)"
"5456","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) liked to begin from the right side in every matter, even when combing his hair and putting on his shoes (he preferred to start from the right side)."
"5457","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wear shoes frequently, for as long as a person keeps wearing shoes, he is like a rider."
"5458","I heard Allah's Apostle ﷺ saying during an expedition in which we also participated: Make a general practice of wearing sandals, for a man is riding as it were when he wears sandals. (Using translation from Muslim 2096)"
"5459","That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Do not walk in one sandal, either wear both sandals, or go barefoot."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1774)"
"5460","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \""No person should walk wearing only one shoe; either wear both shoes or take off both shoes.\"""""
"5461","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: \""Either take both of them off or wear both of them, and when you put on your shoes, put on the right one first, and when you take them off, take off the left one first.\""(Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: \""Take both of them off or wear both of them,\"" is for recommendation and guidanc"
"5462","His nose was cut off at the battle of Al-Kulab during the Jahiliyyah, so he wore a nose made of silver, but it began to rot, so the Prophet [SAW] told him to wear a nose made of gold. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5161)"
"5463","This is how Messenger of Allah ﷺ fumigated. (Using translation from Muslim 2254)"
"5464","The Prophet [SAW] forbade Al-Qaza' (shaving part of the head and leaving part). (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5228)"
"5465","""The Prophet forbade men to perfume themselves with saffron. (Shahih) (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2706)"
"5466","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever has a speck of pride (arrogance) in his heart, shall not be admitted into Paradise. And whoever has a speck of faith in his heart, shall not be admitted in to the Fire.'"" He said: ""So a man said to him: 'I like for my clothes to be nice, and my sandals to be nice?' So he said: 'Indeed Allah loves beauty. But pride is refusing the truth and belittling the people.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1999)"
"5467","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, arrogance is that a person does not accept the truth and looks down upon people."
"5468","I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: The angels do not enter a house which contains a dog or a picture. Zaid b. Khalid al-Juhani said to Sa'id b. Yasar al-Ansari, the transmitter of this tradition: Go with me to 'Aishah, Mother of Faithful, so that we ask about it. So we went and said to her: Mother of Faithful, Abu Talhah has transmitted to us a tradition so-and-so. Have you heard the Prophet ﷺ mentioning that ? She replied: No but I tell what I saw him doing. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went on an expedition and I was waiting for his return. I got a carpet which I hung as a screen on a stick over the door. When he came I received him and said: Peace be upon you, Messenger of Allah, His mercy and His blessings. Praise to be Allah Who gave you dominance and respect. Then he looked at the house and saw the carpet; and he did not respond to me at all. I found (signs of) disapproval in his face. He then came to the carpet and tore it down. He then said: Allah has not commanded us to clothe stones and clay out of the sustenance He has given us. She said: I then cut it to pieces and made two pillows out of it and stuffed them with palm fibre, and he did not disapprove of it to me. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4153)"
"5469","I went to him, I said: (In the narration, these words are:) The color was close to black, so (the teacher narrator) said: I did not say: black."
"5470","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""The Jews and the Christians do not dye (their grey hair), so you shall do the opposite of what they do (i.e. dye your grey hair and beards). (Using translation from Bukhārī 3462)"
"5471","Sayyiduna Abu Quhafa was brought to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The ha"
"5472","Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) brought Sayyiduna Abu Quhafa (may Allah be pleased wi"
"5473","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Change grey hair, and do not resemble the Jews.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 1415)"
"5474","“The best things with which you change gray hair are henna and Katam.”* (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3622)"
"5475","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded to clip the moustaches and grow the beard long. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4199)"
